REPLACE_ME_WITH_A_TYPESAFE_API_KEY

# Copy to secrets/typesafe-api-key, replacing the line above and deleting
# these comments -- the claude launcher (home/programs/claude.nix) strips
# only line endings, not commentary.
#
# Used by the compact-adviser Claude Code plugin, which asks TypeSafe's Jev
# model whether the session is at a safe point to /compact. Installing the
# plugin is consent to send bounded checkpoint context (recent replies and
# clipped tool results, never system prompts or env vars) to
# https://api.typesafe.ai when a key is present.
#
# Mint a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/settings/keys
#
# Without this file the adviser stays inert; /compact-adviser status reports
# "Key: missing". Override at runtime with TYPESAFE_API_KEY.
